+# Result
+
+The original curved orbit undergoes a supercritical bifurcation in the three-dimensional standard critical representation. The exact analytic stationary energy, after complement elimination, has the inherited positive anisotropic quartic. Just above threshold the scalar local quotient has 26 new labeled branches: six balanced 2+2 minima, twelve index-one saddles and eight index-two saddles. The original branch remains unstable above its previously proved threshold.
+
+The new branch radius is sqrt(epsilon), its energy gain is order epsilon^2, with epsilon=kappa/(r*N)-kappa_star(N)/N. The exact curl coefficient is Gamma=((536sqrt10-2624)Lambda_plus+4848sqrt10+18048)/81. Reversibility provides a positive kinetic block and the scalar pair counts; three leading soft squared-frequency formulas include the Gauss-reduced critical mass. Balanced embeddings are orbitally stable at every finite rank for sufficiently small positive epsilon. This does not classify all full-rank stationary states.
+
+Energy preference is not attraction: a strict local minimum of the closed conserved Hamiltonian cannot attract distinct nearby orbits. A sourced preparation/selection law remains open. 66 exact checks and twelve full stationary-energy solves with 42-pair spectra passed. Independent review and the physical bridge remain open; physical promotion 0.
